Experiment patch snapshot: F16 p021 small-ncols pack4

Status: negative, do not promote.
Source tree tested: /home/steve/src/llama.cpp-gemma-record-repro-c926
Source file: ggml/src/ggml-sycl/ggml-sycl.cpp
Gate runs:
  - data/gemma4-q8-gpu0-pack4-control-strict128-20260628Tpack4A/summary.json
  - data/gemma4-q8-gpu1-pack4-enabled-strict128-20260628Tpack4A/summary.json
  - data/gemma4-q8-gpu2-pack4-control-strict128-20260628Tpack4A/summary.json
  - data/gemma4-q8-gpu3-pack4-enabled-strict128-20260628Tpack4A/summary.json

Rationale:
The active Gemma verifier frequently uses the F16 p021 small-token matmul path
with small token columns. This patch tried to compute up to four token columns
inside one workgroup so each F16 weight load could be reused across token
columns.

Patch shape:

1. Add a default-off env gate:

    static bool ggml_sycl_f16_p021_small_ncols_pack4_enabled() {
        const char * env = std::getenv("LLAMA_SYCL_F16_P021_SMALL_NCOLS_PACK4");
        return env && (std::strcmp(env, "1") == 0 ||
                       std::strcmp(env, "true") == 0 ||
                       std::strcmp(env, "TRUE") == 0 ||
                       std::strcmp(env, "yes") == 0 ||
                       std::strcmp(env, "on") == 0);
    }

2. Add a device helper:

    static void mul_mat_p021_f16_f32_small_ncols_pack4(
        const void * __restrict__ vx, const float * __restrict__ y,
        float * __restrict__ dst, const int ncols_x, const int nrows_x,
        const int ncols_y, const int nchannels_x, const int nchannels_y,
        const int row_stride_x, const int channel_stride_x,
        const int token_stride_y, const int channel_stride_y,
        const int token_stride_dst, const int channel_stride_dst,
        const sycl::nd_item<3> &item_ct1)

It used group(0)=channel and group(1)=row_x, then accumulated tmp0..tmp3 for
ncols_y <= 4:

    tmp0 += xi * y[y_base];
    if (ncols_y > 1) tmp1 += xi * y[token_stride_y + y_base];
    if (ncols_y > 2) tmp2 += xi * y[2 * token_stride_y + y_base];
    if (ncols_y > 3) tmp3 += xi * y[3 * token_stride_y + y_base];

Each tmp was reduced through subgroup XOR and written to the corresponding
token-strided dst row.

3. Add host launcher/wrapper:

    ggml_mul_mat_p021_f16_f32_small_ncols_pack4_sycl(...)
    ggml_sycl_mul_mat_vec_p021_small_ncols_pack4(...)

The pack4 launcher used block_nums(nchannels_y, nrows_x, 1), compared with the
existing small-ncols path's block_nums(nchannels_y * ncols_y, nrows_x, 1).

4. Dispatch only when explicitly enabled and safe for the fixed pack width:

    if (ggml_sycl_f16_p021_small_ncols_pack4_enabled() && src1->ne[1] <= 4) {
        ggml_sycl_mul_mat_vec_p021_small_ncols_pack4(ctx, src0, src1, dst);
    } else {
        ggml_sycl_mul_mat_vec_p021_small_ncols(ctx, src0, src1, dst);
    }

Validation:
- Built successfully only after sourcing oneAPI setvars. A raw shell build hit
  host-link missing SYCL/OpenMP symbols; this was a build environment issue.
- Four strict cold 128-token lanes passed canary and realistic final gate
  (`cached_tokens=0`, each prompt once).
- Performance was worse than control:
  - control GPU0: 99.135 tok/s median 1-100
  - pack4 GPU1:   96.377 tok/s median 1-100
  - control GPU2: 95.699 tok/s median 1-100
  - pack4 GPU3:   93.472 tok/s median 1-100

Conclusion:
The single-workgroup pack4 shape likely reduces occupancy/parallelism more
than it saves from reusing the F16 load. Do not promote. The source change was
reverted after preserving this artifact.
